  "summary": "Expert-written benchmarks now test frontier models on biology tasks, while agent systems add bounded orchestration over provenance-tracked data.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is software that imposes domain structure on LLM-driven analysis, favoring bounded, auditable workflows over single-model inference. Fármaco orchestrates drug-screening workflows over a provenance-tracked molecule memory, benchmarked on 22 tasks. The Reasoning Paradox preprint reports that DTDR scaffolding lifts reasoning-LLM accuracy in bioinformatics agent sandboxes from 0% to 9.09% while cutting steps by 66%. SPaRTA provides a text-to-spatial-SQL interface for spatial-omics data with a 7,500-pair benchmark, and BioResearchBench supplies 50 expert-written research tasks for evaluating frontier models on data analysis and interpretation. What is new is provenance-aware, bounded orchestration of LLM agents in analysis pipelines. Performance figures are not comparable across papers, since each uses its own task domain and benchmark.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
